  {
   "say": "Ten Jewish surnames. Ten towns on a map.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Shapiro comes from Speyer, in Germany. In the Middle Ages, it was called Spira.",
   "screen": "Shapiro = *Speyer* (Spira)",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Oppenheimer: Oppenheim. Mintz: Mainz. Landau: Landau.",
   "screen": "Oppenheimer, Mintz, *Landau*",
   "gap": 0.1
  },
  {
   "say": "Halpern: Heilbronn. Ginzburg: Gunzburg.",
   "screen": "Halpern = *Heilbronn.* Ginzburg = *Günzburg.*",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Horowitz: Horovice, in today's Czech Republic.",
   "screen": "Horowitz = *Hořovice*",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Prager: Prague. Wiener: Vienna. Posner: Poznan, Poland.",
   "screen": "Prager, Wiener, *Posner*",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Why towns? In 1787, Austria's emperor ordered every Jew to take a surname.",
   "screen": "*1787:* every Jew needs a surname",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Many simply took the name of the town they came from.",
   "screen": "Name = *home town*",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "But some names hide something much older.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Katz: Hebrew initials for righteous priest.",
   "screen": "Katz = *K*ohen *Tz*edek: righteous priest",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Segal: Hebrew initials for Levite deputy.",
   "screen": "Segal = *Seg*an *L*eviyah: Levite deputy",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Priests and Levites served in the Temple in Jerusalem.",
   "screen": "Back to the *Temple* in Jerusalem",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Not every Shapiro or Katz is Jewish, and family stories vary.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Where does your surname come from? Tell me in the comments.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "If you like Israel facts, follow Noam Roz for more.",
